--- John Johnson wrote:
> la xorxes, your name reminds me of another question: when your lojban 
> name is pronounced, the final s is pronounced too? I assume it must be, 
> since there are no silent letters.

That's right. Names in Lojban have to end in a consonant, so when 
a name that doesn't is lojbanized, either a consonant has to be 
added or final vowels have to be left out. Adding "s" is probably 
the most common choice, but any Lojban consonant will do.

mu'o mi'e xorxes




		
